    "body": "Adds ADR-010, which decides how the cascade combines the three pillars we have already built — the owned DOM (ADR-007), selector matching (ADR-008), and stylesheet parsing (ADR-009) — into a per-element `ComputedStyle`.\n\n## Why\n\nWe can parse a stylesheet and we can match a selector against a node, but we cannot yet answer \"what is the value of `color` for this specific element?\" That is the cascade, and it is the last structural piece before layout and paint.\n\nSame reasoning as ADR-007/008/009 for not delegating to lexbor: its cascade runs on lexbor's own CSS tree, so using it would require reverse-conversion or keeping two trees alive.\n\n## Cascade order (v1)\n\n1. Author declarations marked `!important` beat normal author declarations\n2. Within the same importance level, higher specificity wins\n3. Within the same specificity, later source order wins\n\n## Inheritance (v1)\n\nSeven properties: `color`, `font-family`, `font-size`, `font-style`, `font-weight`, `line-height`, `visibility`. Everything else takes its initial value when no rule applies. Inheritance requires a pre-order DFS: parents must be fully computed before children inherit from them.\n\n## Public API\n\n`cascade(const Stylesheet&, const dom::Document&) -> ComputedStyleMap`\n\nwhere `ComputedStyleMap` is an `unordered_map<const dom::Element*, ComputedStyle>`, and each `ComputedStyle` carries the winning `(value, important, specificity, source_order)` per property.\n\n## Deferred\n\n- UA and user stylesheets (v1 is author stylesheet only)\n- `@media` queries, `@layer` cascade layers\n- `var()`, custom properties, `calc()`\n- Shorthand expansion (`margin: 0 1em` stays raw)\n- Typed computed values (`Length`, `Color`, `Keyword`)\n- DOM mutation invalidation\n\n## Consequences\n\n- New files: `src/renderer/css/cascade.hpp`, `cascade.cpp`, `tests/test_cascade.cpp`\n- No new lexbor includes — ADR-007 isolation invariant still holds\n- `renderer::dom` and `renderer::css::SelectorList` untouched\n\n## Next\n\nOnce ADR-010 merges, the implementation issue will be \"Implement the cascade per ADR-010\" — two commits (matching + specificity ordering, then inheritance + typed getters), same rhythm as #103.\n",
